# UST.G3FF: H02 Component-20 Conic Fourth-Normal Source Theorem

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_QGAMMA_CONIC_QUOTIENT_AND_48_FIBER_FOURTH_NORMAL_PROFILE_INTERTWINER_OPEN`

This theorem combines one exact characteristic-zero source identity with an
independent exact finite-field normal-filtration campaign. It does not yet
identify the full characteristic-zero endpoint quotient with the displayed
normal carrier.

## Setup

Let

```text
q = xz - y^2
```

be the selected root conic in the G3BI start member. Its root graph is

```text
Rminus: q = 0,  w = -G3(x,y,z).
```

The G3BI root-containment correction supplies three degree-nine coefficient
rows `A0,A1,A2` over `Q(gamma)`. The canonical component-20 split kernels from
G3DI--G3DU are

```text
K_15 subset Sym^15(k^3),  dim K_15 = 100,
```

at six roots over each of eight independent split primes.

## Exact Source Identity

After the literal substitution `w=-G3`, coefficientwise division over the
six-coordinate power basis of `Q(gamma)` gives

```text
(A0-A1)|_(w=-G3) = q D7,
```

where

```text
D7 in Sym^7(Q(gamma)^3),
dim Sym^7 = 36.
```

The stored coefficient table has shape `36 x 6`; 35 of its 36 monomial rows
are nonzero and its largest absolute power-basis coordinate is 590. Every one
of the six integer-coordinate divisions has zero remainder. Thus this part is
an exact identity over `Q(gamma)`, not a modular reconstruction.

## Conic Normal Filtration

For each split fiber define

```text
K_j = {f in Sym^(15-2j)(k^3) : q^j f lies in K_15}.
```

All 48 canonical fibers have exactly the same dimensions:

```text
j:          0   1   2   3  4  5  6  7
dim K_j:  100  69  42  19  0  0  0  0.
```

The successive dimensions are therefore

```text
31, 27, 23, 19,
```

which are the full restriction dimensions on the conic in degrees
`30,26,22,18`. In particular,

```text
100 = 31 + 27 + 23 + 19.
```

At normal order four the intersection vanishes, and direct rank computation
on every fiber proves

```text
K_15 direct_sum q^4 Sym^7(k^3) = Sym^15(k^3).
```

The complementary dimension is

```text
136 - 100 = 36 = dim Sym^7.
```

